  "u2-l4.0.title": {
    "en": "Verbs: an ending for each person",
    "t": "Feʼllar: har bir shaxsga oʻz qoʻshimchasi"
  },
  "u2-l4.0.body": {
    "en": [
      "Slovak verbs change their ending to show who is doing something: **-m** (I), **-š** (you), no ending (he, she), **-me** (we), **-te** (you), and **-jú**, **-ú** or **-ia** (they).",
      "Like hovoriť: **robiť** (to do) → robím, robíš, robí… Čo robíš? = What do you do?",
      "Languages go with **po**: hovoriť po slovensky (Slovak), po anglicky (English), po nemecky (German)."
    ],
    "t": [
      "Slovak feʼllari ham, oʻzbek feʼllari kabi, kim bajarayotganini qoʻshimcha bilan koʻrsatadi: **-m** (men), **-š** (sen), qoʻshimchasiz (u), **-me** (biz), **-te** (siz) va **-jú**, **-ú** yoki **-ia** (ular). Solishtiring: hovorí**m** — gapiraman.",
      "Xuddi hovoriť kabi: **robiť** (qilmoq) → robím, robíš, robí… Čo robíš? = Nima ish qilasan?",
      "Tillar **po** bilan aytiladi: hovoriť po slovensky (slovakcha gapirmoq), po anglicky (inglizcha), po nemecky (nemischa)."
    ]
  },
  "u2-l4.0.table.head": {
